{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Protected data choice: `y` is the only top-level data variable scored by a sampling statement (`y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y)`). The remaining data variables are context inputs used for sizes and indexing.

Changes: added explicit built-in `uniform(0, 100)` priors for `sigma_a`, `sigma_b`, and `sigma_y`, matching their finite parameter constraints. This satisfies SafeStan's unique-prior requirement for all parameters without changing the intended posterior. No data fields were added or reshaped.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  int<lower=0> n_groups;
  int<lower=0> n_scenarios;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=n_groups> group_id;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=n_scenarios> scenario_id;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  vector[n_groups] eta_a;
  vector[n_scenarios] eta_b;
  real mu_a;
  real mu_b;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_a;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_b;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_y;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[N] y_hat;
  vector[n_groups] a;
  vector[n_scenarios] b;

  a = 10 * mu_a + eta_a * sigma_a;
  b = 10 * mu_b + eta_b * sigma_b;

  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = a[group_id[i]] + b[scenario_id[i]];
  }
}
model {
  mu_a ~ normal(0, 1);
  eta_a ~ normal(0, 1);

  mu_b ~ normal(0, 1);
  eta_b ~ normal(0, 1);

  sigma_a ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_b ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100);

  y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":1,"group_id":[2],"n_groups":2,"n_scenarios":4,"scenario_id":[2],"y":[1.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
